# HakiOS fragment: Qualcomm SM8250 ("kona": Snapdragon 865 / 865+, with the SDX55 modem) -- what is
# true of the SoC, whatever phone it is in.
#
# Eight cores: cpu0-3 are Cortex-A55 (the little cluster), cpu4-6 Cortex-A77 (the gold cluster) and
# cpu7 a Cortex-A77 at the prime clock -- so the biggest core is 7, as on the reference phone.
# Read from this phone's own device tree (/cpus/cpu@0 ... cpu@700: "arm,cortex-a55"/"arm,cortex-a77").
#
# The SoC's drivers (CPUFREQ, THERMAL, PMIC, SOCINFO) are NOT here yet: the ones in the common tree
# were written for the SC7280 family's registers and neither their addresses nor their clock plan
# are kona's. The device fragment leaves them out until a kona version exists (docs/port-checklist.md,
# step 3, order 1). What kona's addresses are, where they differ from the kernel's sc7280 defaults,
# and which of them travel as boot-arguments, is in docs/device-report.md and soc.args.
CONFIG_SOC="sm8250"
CONFIG_CPUS=8
CONFIG_BOOTCPU=7
